commune by followers of the Indian  spiritual guru Bhagwan Shree Rajneesh in  1981 and the grim events which took  place after things began to spiral out  of control the series tells this bizarre  and frightening tale in a slow and  precise manner with plenty of archival  footage and interviews with former  followers of Rajneesh many of whom were  close knit members of a group known for  its mass stockpiling of weapons heavy  reliance on arson and penchant for  poisoning salad bars it's not to be  missed  worst mute mute had everything going for  it the cast included a host of stars  like Justin Theroux Paul Rudd and  Alexander Skarsgard it was co-written  and directed by Duncan Jones the mind  behind modern-day sci-fi classics like  moon and source code even the premise a  mute bartender searching for his missing  love and a futuristic Berlin seemed like  it was full of potential  but when mute finally hit Netflix in  2018 bands were left disappointed  Rosie Fletcher of Digital Spy summarized  the movie best saying the whole film is  populated by people you don't believe or  care at all about behaving in ways that  don't make sense again state  cheap-looking sci-fi by numbers  background  best a futile and stupid gesture on its  surface it's the story at the beginning  of the National Lampoon the premiere  humor magazine of the 1970s and early  80s but a futile and stupid gesture is  also the life story of his co-founder  Doug Kenney tempting but he flatly saw  the light the Lampoon was an incredibly  influential brand staffed by personnel  who went on to produce a range of iconic  comedies including Caddyshack and Animal  House the cast is bursting with comedy  stars all paying tribute to their heroes  Joel McHale portrays his community  co-star Chevy Chase while Seth Green  pops up as Christopher Guest Will Forte  is a revelation here too turning in an  oscar-worthy performance as Kenny a  gifted comic genius who suffers at the  whims of his own demons even as he goes  on to change the world  yeah so these actors don't look exactly  like the real people but come on you  think I look like Will Forte when I was  27 do you think Will Forte is 27  worst game over man if you weren't a fan  of the long-running Comedy Central  sitcom workaholics you're probably not  going to find much to love here game  over man takes everything that was  thrown into that show and dials it up to  11 jokes about genitalia tons of them  romanticized 80s action movie violence  endless irreverent profanity-laden  banter between the three leads you  betcha  the movies thin plot is essentially a  dull rehash of diehard which isn't  enough to mask the fact that onder's  home Blake Anderson and Adam Devine are  still portraying the exact same  character types they played on  workaholics great if you love that show  not so great if you didn't altered  carbon based on the 2002 novel by  Richard K Morgan altered carbon is set  in a far-flung future in which  scientists can upload a person's  memories onto an implantable disc it's  essentially a highly stylized crime  story filled to the brim with  body-switching  sci-fi tech and murder 5 most frequently  murdered  allows me being in AI makes that less  likely no although both tremendously  violent and sexually charged altered  urban also explores identity on a  philosophical level that sci-fi hasn't  matched since the matrix worst the week  of the week of places the now fifty year  old Adam Sandler and the doofus dad  phase of his career while giving us a  new Sandler to go along with silly  Sandler and serious actor Sandler boring  Sandler Isaac likes Jimmy Lee and he's  aware that Jimmy Lin no longer plays for  the New York Knicks it's a very nice  shirt $7.00 at motels seriously furry  little happens in this movie it takes  place during the week of his daughter's  wedding to the son of a surgeon played  probably unsurprisingly by Chris Rock  Sandler gets into some slapstick messes  up preparations for the